    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Vulnerability refers to the predisposition/propensity of exposed elements such as human beings, their livelihoods, and assets to be adversely affected by a natural hazard. This element contributes to and encompasses a variety of concepts and elements, including sensitivity or susceptibility to harm and/or lack of capacity to prevent, prepare, respond, cope and/or adapt (IPCC, 2021)."
